{
  "abstract": "If Σ a(n) x^n/n! = F(x) exp(x G(x)) with F, G integer power series and G(0) = 1, then a(n+k) ≡ a(n) (mod k) for all n, k (Bala 2017, Theorem 1). Hence A000262 (exp(x/(1−x))) and A082579 (exp(x/(1−x)^2)) satisfy k | a(n+k) − a(n) for k >= 2.",
